1. **A centrifugal separator comprising:**

a rotatable separation chamber configured to rotate about an axis and to separate a feed mixture into at least a first fraction and a second fraction;

at least one inlet fluidly coupled to the separation chamber for introducing the feed mixture into the separation chamber;

a first outlet fluidly coupled to a first region of the separation chamber for discharging the first fraction;

a second outlet fluidly coupled to a second region of the separation chamber for discharging the second fraction; and

an intermittent discharge system associated with the second outlet and operable between a closed state, in which the intermittent discharge system seals the second outlet while the separation chamber rotates, and an open state, in which accumulated second fraction is discharged through the second outlet, the intermittent discharge system being configured to return to the closed state after each discharge.
